### Large Group $export — see config/large-export.yaml for setup.
#
# $export is asynchronous: the POST returns 202 at once with a status URL in
# Content-Location; poll it until it answers 200 with the manifest, then
# download each file. Run the requests below in order.

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@base = {{host}}/r4

### 1. Create a group: every patient with a final Observation
# @name createGroup
POST {{base}}/Group
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Group",
  "type": "person",
  "actual": true,
  "name": "Large export - patients with a final Observation",
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/bulkdata/StructureDefinition/member-filter",
      "valueString": "Observation?status=final"
    }
  ]
}

### 2. Kick off the export (returns 202 immediately; copy the Content-Location header)
# @name kickoff
POST {{base}}/Group/{{createGroup.response.body.$.id}}/$export?_type=Patient,Observation
Prefer: respond-async

### 3. Poll: 202 + X-Progress while running, 200 + manifest when done,
###    or the failure's own status + OperationOutcome if it failed
GET {{host}}{{kickoff.response.headers.Content-Location}}

### 4. Download a file from the manifest (streamed from disk)
GET {{host}}/r4/$export-files/dfcb4d3a-809b-4357-b039-94a69b0151a3/Observation.ndjson

### 5. Cancel a running export / discard a finished one
DELETE {{host}}{{kickoff.response.headers.Content-Location}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Paged search: _count/_offset page the result in SQL; the Bundle carries
### `total` and a `next` link while more follows.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### First page of 500 Observations
GET {{base}}/Observation?status=final&_count=500
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Third page
GET {{base}}/Observation?status=final&_count=500&_offset=1000
Accept: application/fhir+json
